1
00:00:00,420 --> 00:00:02,980
Now the penalty kicks begin.

2
00:00:03,330 --> 00:00:06,980
Five players from each team will take the penalty kicks.

3
00:00:07,670 --> 00:00:12,490
If the tie is not broken, the kicks will continue until one team gains the advantage.

4
00:00:12,930 --> 00:00:18,490
Will the goddess of victory smile upon Japan or France?

5
00:00:19,180 --> 00:00:23,400
Japan's goalkeeper Wakashimazu-kun takes his place in the goal.

6
00:00:33,870 --> 00:00:38,750
CAPTAIN TSUBASA: JUNIOR YOUTH ARC

7
00:01:54,430 --> 00:02:00,940
EPISODE 26: MIRACLE PUNCH

8
00:01:54,640 --> 00:01:56,850
Pierre, Pierre!

9
00:01:57,010 --> 00:01:58,940
Pierre, Pierre!

10
00:01:59,020 --> 00:02:00,940
Pierre, Pierre!

11
00:02:01,110 --> 00:02:03,270
Pierre, Pierre!

12
00:02:03,360 --> 00:02:05,530
Pierre, Pierre!

13
00:02:05,610 --> 00:02:08,940
Pierre, Pierre!

14
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:10,690
Score, Pierre!

15
00:02:10,870 --> 00:02:12,940
We believe in you, Wakashimazu.

16
00:02:12,940 --> 00:02:14,940
It's no different from what you always do.

17
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:16,940
Wakashimazu, catch it!

18
00:02:17,370 --> 00:02:20,290
Japan's goalkeeper, Wakashimazu-kun.

19
00:02:20,380 --> 00:02:23,340
Under normal circumstances, saving penalties is his strong suit.

20
00:02:24,460 --> 00:02:29,210
Let's hope his injured hand and fatigue don't slow his reaction too much.

21
00:02:29,510 --> 00:02:31,510
I lost the previous penalty kick...

22
00:02:31,590 --> 00:02:34,460
because he deceived me with his footwork.

23
00:02:35,310 --> 00:02:36,890
Good, the right side.

24
00:02:38,980 --> 00:02:40,900
This time will be different.

25
00:02:44,650 --> 00:02:48,390
With the cheers of his supporters, Pierre-kun makes his move.

26
00:02:51,070 --> 00:02:53,400
To the opposite side of where his standing foot points!

27
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:54,900
Come on!

28
00:02:56,900 --> 00:03:00,540
Goal! It went exactly where his standing foot pointed.

29
00:03:00,620 --> 00:03:02,960
Wakashimazu-kun dove the wrong way!

30
00:03:03,040 --> 00:03:04,410
D-Damn it!

31
00:03:04,630 --> 00:03:07,410
France scored first and took a 1-0 lead.

32
00:03:07,410 --> 00:03:09,670
Alright guys, follow me.

33
00:03:09,760 --> 00:03:10,910
Okay!

34
00:03:11,180 --> 00:03:12,720
France's famous captain,

35
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:16,670
El Sid Pierre-kun, converted the first penalty.

36
00:03:16,850 --> 00:03:21,430
Will Japan's first penalty be taken by captain Tsubasa-kun as well?

37
00:03:21,430 --> 00:03:24,520
Amoros, Amoros, Amoros!

38
00:03:24,610 --> 00:03:27,570
Amoros, Amoros, Amoros!

39
00:03:27,650 --> 00:03:28,860
Amoros, Amoros!

40
00:03:28,940 --> 00:03:33,200
Japan's first penalty taker is Hyuga-kun.

41
00:03:33,280 --> 00:03:36,080
Kojiro Hyuga-kun, Japan's best forward.

42
00:03:36,120 --> 00:03:39,190
He must definitely feel the pressure being chosen as the first penalty taker.

43
00:03:41,750 --> 00:03:43,880
Japan's first penalty taker is Hyuga.

44
00:03:43,960 --> 00:03:45,200
I trust you!

45
00:03:45,750 --> 00:03:47,080
Kojiro.

46
00:03:47,380 --> 00:03:51,050
All the fans are chanting goalkeeper Amoros' name in unison.

47
00:03:51,130 --> 00:03:53,010
The home crowd

48
00:03:53,090 --> 00:03:55,080
wants their team to advance to the final.

49
00:03:58,060 --> 00:03:59,310
Miss it!

50
00:03:59,390 --> 00:04:00,590
I hope you mess up!

51
00:04:07,820 --> 00:04:13,600
Apparently, they don't want him to score.

52
00:04:16,200 --> 00:04:17,110
Tsubasa.

53
00:04:17,370 --> 00:04:21,250
Hyuga-kun, ignore them, just do your job.

54
00:04:21,790 --> 00:04:22,710
Okay.

55
00:04:33,620 --> 00:04:39,430
Hyuga-kun's left leg is injured, but will he be able to shoot?

56
00:04:41,390 --> 00:04:42,590
This...

57
00:04:42,590 --> 00:04:44,190
is all my strength.

58
00:04:44,270 --> 00:04:47,010
Tiger Shot!

59
00:04:50,190 --> 00:04:52,350
Goal!

60
00:04:52,740 --> 00:04:54,030
In the net!

61
00:04:54,110 --> 00:04:57,160
The ball goes right into the center of the goal.

62
00:04:57,240 --> 00:05:00,610
Goalkeeper Amoros-kun couldn't even move!

63
00:05:01,160 --> 00:05:03,110
S-So fast.

64
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:06,040
Hyuga-kun scores very comfortably!

65
00:05:06,120 --> 00:05:08,670
His injured leg didn't stop him from taking a hard shot!

66
00:05:08,750 --> 00:05:12,120
Hyuga-kun takes a decisive and unstoppable penalty kick!

67
00:05:12,420 --> 00:05:15,870
France and Japan each scored one, the score is 1-1.

68
00:05:16,260 --> 00:05:17,880
Good, I did it.

69
00:05:18,180 --> 00:05:20,180
Your shot was great, Hyuga-kun.

70
00:05:20,260 --> 00:05:21,880
The score is now 1-1.

71
00:05:22,140 --> 00:05:25,020
Bossi-kun, France's second penalty taker.

72
00:05:25,640 --> 00:05:29,730
Now they shift from chanting "Amoros" to chanting "Bossi".

73
00:05:30,230 --> 00:05:31,890
I'll catch it this time!

74
00:05:32,110 --> 00:05:33,820
Come on, let's support them too, guys.

75
00:05:33,900 --> 00:05:36,640
Good luck! You can do it, Japan's goalkeeper!

76
00:05:38,110 --> 00:05:39,400
Very strange.

77
00:05:39,740 --> 00:05:42,990
The match should have been over long before now.

78
00:05:45,750 --> 00:05:46,900
Please, my dear hand.

79
00:05:47,170 --> 00:05:48,910
Bossi-kun takes his shot!

80
00:05:52,880 --> 00:05:55,660
Oh, Wakashimazu-kun stops it!

81
00:05:55,840 --> 00:05:56,920
What?

82
00:06:00,260 --> 00:06:01,300
Wakashimazu!

83
00:06:01,390 --> 00:06:02,430
I got away with it.

84
00:06:02,510 --> 00:06:04,560
Oh, it didn't work.

85
00:06:04,640 --> 00:06:06,560
It seemed like it was caught but...

86
00:06:06,640 --> 00:06:10,610
Apparently, Wakashimazu-kun's right hand has lost too much strength.

87
00:06:10,690 --> 00:06:13,180
He touched it with his palm, but it still became a goal.

88
00:06:13,180 --> 00:06:16,680
The second penalty is successful, the score is 2-1 in France's favor.

89
00:06:16,990 --> 00:06:18,570
I did it, guys.

90
00:06:18,650 --> 00:06:19,690
Great, Bossi.

91
00:06:20,280 --> 00:06:22,580
Wakashimazu-kun would normally have caught that.

92
00:06:22,660 --> 00:06:24,830
This must be painful for Japan.

93
00:06:25,290 --> 00:06:26,940
D-Damn it.

94
00:06:27,620 --> 00:06:29,450
Wakashimazu.

95
00:06:31,710 --> 00:06:34,550
Don't lose, keep fighting, Wakashimazu.

96
00:06:35,880 --> 00:06:38,840
Who is Japan's second penalty taker?

97
00:06:41,140 --> 00:06:43,140
Matsuyama-kun.

98
00:06:43,220 --> 00:06:47,340
Just like when he played in Furano, he puts on his headband.

99
00:06:50,590 --> 00:06:54,270
France converted both of their penalties.

100
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:56,940
Japan must not fall into despair.

101
00:06:57,100 --> 00:07:02,600
Will Matsuyama-kun be able to convert the penalty like Hyuga-kun?

102
00:07:02,820 --> 00:07:04,740
With these penalty kicks,

103
00:07:04,830 --> 00:07:08,500
we fight on behalf of all the Japanese players who couldn't come here.

104
00:07:08,620 --> 00:07:10,460
I can't miss this.

105
00:07:15,420 --> 00:07:21,370
And for Soda, I will convert this penalty at all costs!

106
00:07:24,430 --> 00:07:26,180
Eagle Shot!

107
00:07:34,980 --> 00:07:36,230
Goal!

108
00:07:36,320 --> 00:07:41,770
The penalty shootout between Japan and France is now 2-2.

109
00:07:42,280 --> 00:07:45,660
Amoros-kun dove the right way, but Matsuyama-kun's Eagle Shot

110
00:07:45,740 --> 00:07:50,200
hit the net just before he could reach it.

111
00:07:50,290 --> 00:07:51,710
Matsuyama-kun.

112
00:07:52,250 --> 00:07:57,790
Michel Ferreri, France's third penalty taker.

113
00:07:57,800 --> 00:07:59,880
Ferreri! Ferreri!

114
00:07:59,960 --> 00:08:02,010
Ferreri! Ferreri!

115
00:08:02,090 --> 00:08:05,720
But what is the condition of Wakashimazu-kun's right hand right now?

116
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:07,260
Will he really be able to catch a shot?

117
00:08:07,800 --> 00:08:09,520
You can do it, Wakashimazu.

118
00:08:09,600 --> 00:08:11,300
You will catch this!

119
00:08:11,930 --> 00:08:14,100
Ferreri! Ferreri!

120
00:08:14,190 --> 00:08:16,360
Ferreri! Ferreri!

121
00:08:16,440 --> 00:08:19,610
Ferreri! Ferreri! Ferreri!

122
00:08:19,690 --> 00:08:23,150
Ferreri-kun makes his move and takes the shot!

123
00:08:25,820 --> 00:08:31,450
Goal! In the net! France makes it 3-2.

124
00:08:33,410 --> 00:08:37,070
It didn't work, without my right hand I can't stop them.

125
00:08:39,880 --> 00:08:41,340
Well done, Ferreri.

126
00:08:41,420 --> 00:08:42,830
Great shot!

127
00:08:43,340 --> 00:08:45,180
To protect his injured hand,

128
00:08:45,260 --> 00:08:48,430
Wakashimazu-kun tried to catch with his left hand.

129
00:08:48,510 --> 00:08:50,970
But he couldn't reach it.

130
00:08:51,430 --> 00:08:54,310
France is ahead again, and Japan is under pressure.

131
00:08:54,390 --> 00:08:55,720
And the third penalty taker...

132
00:08:56,560 --> 00:08:58,440
Oh, it's Misaki-kun.

133
00:08:58,520 --> 00:09:02,220
Taro Misaki-kun takes the third kick.

134
00:09:07,200 --> 00:09:08,280
Taro.

135
00:09:08,730 --> 00:09:11,740
Good luck! Just ignore them.

136
00:09:11,830 --> 00:09:13,740
Misaki-kun, score.

137
00:09:16,250 --> 00:09:18,290
I can't miss this.

138
00:09:18,710 --> 00:09:24,510
Otherwise, this match will be my last one with the guys.

139
00:09:25,170 --> 00:09:27,760
I want to play one more match with them.

140
00:09:28,680 --> 00:09:32,500
I want to play against Germany with them in the final.

141
00:09:32,970 --> 00:09:37,690
This tournament helped me make my decision at its end.

142
00:09:38,350 --> 00:09:42,190
I have been struggling with this issue since I came here.

143
00:09:42,940 --> 00:09:47,520
No matter how many years it takes for my father to return to Japan to paint Mount Fuji...

144
00:09:47,520 --> 00:09:52,370
I will continue to wear this flag and play for my country as a Japanese citizen.

145
00:09:53,080 --> 00:09:56,530
Now the time of doubt is over.

146
00:09:56,910 --> 00:10:01,670
For the rest of my life, I want to play for Japan together with Tsubasa-kun and the others.

147
00:10:03,210 --> 00:10:06,040
Misaki-kun goes to take his shot.

148
00:10:06,550 --> 00:10:07,720
Misaki-kun.

149
00:10:08,470 --> 00:10:10,470
CAPTAIN TSUBASA: JUNIOR YOUTH ARC

150
00:10:14,700 --> 00:10:17,050
Birthday: December 29 | Height: 172 cm | Weight: 60 kg | Blood Type: A

151
00:10:25,180 --> 00:10:29,670
Misaki-kun scores from the left corner!

152
00:10:29,760 --> 00:10:31,380
Goalkeeper Amoros-kun couldn't reach it!

153
00:10:31,470 --> 00:10:33,090
What wonderful control!

154
00:10:33,180 --> 00:10:34,260
Great!

155
00:10:35,940 --> 00:10:37,810
Great shot, Misaki-kun.

156
00:10:37,890 --> 00:10:40,350
- Well done! - Misaki-kun!

157
00:10:40,440 --> 00:10:42,700
Thanks, guys.

158
00:10:42,940 --> 00:10:45,270
And the score becomes 3-3 again.

159
00:10:45,360 --> 00:10:46,940
Neither side missed!

160
00:10:47,030 --> 00:10:49,490
The tension continues.

161
00:10:49,900 --> 00:10:54,960
France's fourth penalty taker is Jean Roost-kun.

162
00:10:54,960 --> 00:10:57,720
Roost! Roost! Roost!

163
00:10:58,080 --> 00:10:59,330
I'll catch it.

164
00:10:59,410 --> 00:11:01,720
I don't need my palm, I just have to clear it.

165
00:11:01,720 --> 00:11:03,750
I'll stop it with my right hand.

166
00:11:04,460 --> 00:11:07,210
Japan must stop this!

167
00:11:07,300 --> 00:11:10,230
The wounded lion, goalkeeper Wakashimazu-kun,

168
00:11:10,630 --> 00:11:13,230
continues his struggle.

169
00:11:13,470 --> 00:11:16,100
Roost! Roost! Roost!

170
00:11:16,180 --> 00:11:17,640
Roost! Roost!

171
00:11:17,720 --> 00:11:20,020
Which way will Roost-kun shoot?

172
00:11:20,100 --> 00:11:22,190
They know that Wakashimazu-kun is injured.

173
00:11:22,270 --> 00:11:26,730
And so far, they have shot to the right side of the goal three times.

174
00:11:26,810 --> 00:11:28,500
What will Roost-kun do?

175
00:11:28,820 --> 00:11:31,190
This time, definitely the right side.

176
00:11:31,400 --> 00:11:35,750
Goalkeeper Wakashimazu-kun seems to have guessed this and dives right.

177
00:11:36,990 --> 00:11:38,990
Oh, this went to the left!

178
00:11:39,080 --> 00:11:41,760
To Wakashimazu-kun's opposite direction.

179
00:11:41,870 --> 00:11:43,040
Damn.

180
00:11:43,120 --> 00:11:45,920
France didn't miss.

181
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:48,590
Just like in their training.

182
00:11:48,670 --> 00:11:51,520
They carefully send the ball into the goal from the corners.

183
00:11:51,760 --> 00:11:54,020
Great, Roost! Well done!

184
00:11:54,800 --> 00:11:59,850
It seems captain Pierre-kun is telling them the direction of the shots.

185
00:12:00,030 --> 00:12:03,690
Japan's fourth penalty taker is Misugi-kun.

186
00:12:03,890 --> 00:12:05,980
Despite having a heart condition,

187
00:12:06,060 --> 00:12:10,190
and despite having no chance of substitution, he fought to the end.

188
00:12:10,290 --> 00:12:13,240
He is Jun Misugi-kun.

189
00:12:13,320 --> 00:12:17,120
Officially, Japan's fourth penalty taker.

190
00:12:17,530 --> 00:12:20,240
Misugi asked for this himself.

191
00:12:20,330 --> 00:12:23,050
Then I trust you, score.

192
00:12:23,330 --> 00:12:25,550
Jun! Jun...

193
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:28,130
Are you okay, Misugi?

194
00:12:28,170 --> 00:12:29,310
Misugi-kun.

195
00:12:30,380 --> 00:12:33,260
I'm fine, just sit and watch.

196
00:12:33,420 --> 00:12:38,430
This is my last task in this tournament, don't worry.

197
00:12:42,020 --> 00:12:43,180
I feel it.

198
00:12:43,560 --> 00:12:44,770
I hear its voice.

199
00:12:44,930 --> 00:12:49,580
Whenever I play, my heart grows even stronger.

200
00:12:54,530 --> 00:12:55,400
Get ready!

201
00:12:55,370 --> 00:12:58,990
Misugi-kun makes his move and shoots!

202
00:13:02,340 --> 00:13:07,590
Goal! He skillfully sends the ball into the net from the left!

203
00:13:07,870 --> 00:13:09,600
Great shot, Jun!

204
00:13:10,040 --> 00:13:11,090
He did it!

205
00:13:11,170 --> 00:13:12,350
Great!

206
00:13:12,590 --> 00:13:17,860
Misugi-kun brilliantly completes his mission in this game.

207
00:13:18,840 --> 00:13:21,980
Wakashimazu-kun, I did it.

208
00:13:22,310 --> 00:13:23,510
Misugi.

209
00:13:26,490 --> 00:13:28,140
Napoleon!

210
00:13:28,230 --> 00:13:31,490
France's fifth penalty taker is Napoleon-kun!

211
00:13:31,730 --> 00:13:36,250
Undoubtedly, Japan will now send their captain Tsubasa-kun.

212
00:13:36,610 --> 00:13:39,000
I trust you, Napoleon.

213
00:13:39,660 --> 00:13:40,700
Yes.

214
00:13:42,200 --> 00:13:44,120
If these two fail to score,

215
00:13:44,200 --> 00:13:45,950
then they will take turns one by one after that.

216
00:13:46,040 --> 00:13:48,290
And the kicks will continue until one gains the advantage.

217
00:13:48,370 --> 00:13:51,170
From this perspective, the fifth penalty taker is very important.

218
00:13:54,300 --> 00:13:56,210
Japan's goalkeeper.

219
00:13:56,300 --> 00:14:00,800
How dare you prevent me from getting a third hat-trick!?

220
00:14:01,010 --> 00:14:04,760
But I won't give up on being the top scorer.

221
00:14:04,850 --> 00:14:07,430
There is only a 2-goal difference between Schneider and me.

222
00:14:07,520 --> 00:14:10,900
I will completely surpass him in the final.

223
00:14:12,440 --> 00:14:15,290
Now or never, I'll go to the right side again.

224
00:14:15,690 --> 00:14:19,290
If Misugi can risk his life...

225
00:14:19,450 --> 00:14:21,820
then why can't my hand risk itself?

226
00:14:25,660 --> 00:14:28,040
Napoleon-kun starts his run-up.

227
00:14:28,710 --> 00:14:32,050
Say goodbye to that right hand now.

228
00:14:32,500 --> 00:14:34,560
Napoleon-kun takes the shot!

229
00:14:34,710 --> 00:14:38,480
Catch, here it comes, Cannon Shot!

230
00:14:43,680 --> 00:14:45,940
You want my hand? Just try it!

231
00:14:46,180 --> 00:14:48,700
Karate punch!

232
00:14:51,390 --> 00:14:52,520
He stopped it!

233
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:57,200
Wakashimazu-kun's karate punch destroyed Napoleon-kun's Cannon Shot.

234
00:14:57,230 --> 00:14:58,280
What!?

235
00:14:58,360 --> 00:15:01,210
Finally, France missed a penalty.

236
00:15:01,610 --> 00:15:04,740
Wakashimazu-kun overcomes his injury!

237
00:15:04,820 --> 00:15:08,720
He makes a golden save with his right hand!

238
00:15:08,720 --> 00:15:11,750
Did you see? I stopped him!

239
00:15:12,960 --> 00:15:16,720
The karate goalkeeper Wakashimazu-kun is still standing.

240
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:18,230
Wakashimazu!

241
00:15:18,230 --> 00:15:19,760
He-He did it!

242
00:15:19,840 --> 00:15:21,150
Just what you'd expect from him!

243
00:15:21,550 --> 00:15:23,810
Well done, Wakashimazu.

244
00:15:23,810 --> 00:15:27,820
Finally, Wakashimazu-kun stops the fifth shot.

245
00:15:27,810 --> 00:15:32,770
Not only that, he stops the shot of France's best forward, Napoleon-kun!

246
00:15:32,850 --> 00:15:34,580
I-Impossible.

247
00:15:35,480 --> 00:15:37,080
Napoleon.

248
00:15:38,780 --> 00:15:41,080
Great defense, Wakashimazu.

249
00:15:41,740 --> 00:15:44,610
My right hand has now given up.

250
00:15:44,990 --> 00:15:47,590
I leave the rest to you, Tsubasa.

251
00:15:48,160 --> 00:15:53,500
And the fifth penalty taker, the captain of the Japan youth team,

252
00:15:53,580 --> 00:15:55,600
Ozora Tsubasa-kun steps forward.

253
00:15:56,170 --> 00:15:57,750
You were great, Wakashimazu.

254
00:15:57,840 --> 00:16:01,710
You went all out and forgot about your injury.

255
00:16:01,800 --> 00:16:03,350
I will not let this fighting spirit go to waste.

256
00:16:03,550 --> 00:16:04,430
Tsubasa!

257
00:16:04,510 --> 00:16:05,590
We trust you.

258
00:16:05,680 --> 00:16:07,610
France missed the fifth.

259
00:16:07,970 --> 00:16:09,850
Japan took 4 penalties.

260
00:16:09,930 --> 00:16:14,620
Hyuga-kun, Matsuyama-kun, Misaki-kun, and Misugi-kun all scored.

261
00:16:14,850 --> 00:16:19,620
If Tsubasa-kun scores, Japan wins and advances to the final.

262
00:16:19,980 --> 00:16:21,110
Tsubasa!

263
00:16:21,190 --> 00:16:22,370
Tsubasa-kun.

264
00:16:22,530 --> 00:16:23,570
Score!

265
00:16:23,650 --> 00:16:25,820
Tsubasa-senpai, don't miss!

266
00:16:25,910 --> 00:16:27,130
Tsubasa-kun.

267
00:16:27,370 --> 00:16:30,410
Miss it, miss it!

268
00:16:31,130 --> 00:16:36,890
It's no surprise that the home crowd wants Tsubasa-kun to miss his penalty.

269
00:16:37,040 --> 00:16:41,340
Miss! Miss! Miss!

270
00:16:45,760 --> 00:16:47,650
The ball is my friend.

271
00:16:50,850 --> 00:16:53,400
Tsubasa-kun is smiling.

272
00:16:53,730 --> 00:16:54,850
It's over.

273
00:16:54,930 --> 00:16:57,690
Japan won, Coach Barbas.

274
00:16:59,410 --> 00:17:01,870
Tsubasa-kun starts his run-up.

275
00:17:03,400 --> 00:17:04,330
Get ready!

276
00:17:05,360 --> 00:17:07,360
Tsubasa-kun takes the shot!

277
00:17:08,840 --> 00:17:10,700
Amoros-kun dives to the left!

278
00:17:11,740 --> 00:17:13,750
And the ball goes to the left too!

279
00:17:26,720 --> 00:17:30,390
Tsubasa-kun's extraordinary shot hits the net from the left.

280
00:17:30,680 --> 00:17:33,600
Go-Goal! Japan!

281
00:17:33,680 --> 00:17:38,240
They win the penalty shootout 5-4 and advance to the final!

282
00:17:38,240 --> 00:17:40,650
We did it! We did it!

283
00:17:41,230 --> 00:17:46,250
In the most critical moments, Tsubasa-kun never misses.

284
00:17:46,490 --> 00:17:47,400
Tsubasa!

285
00:17:47,490 --> 00:17:50,990
We won! We won, Wakashimazu! It's thanks to you!

286
00:17:51,120 --> 00:17:53,740
We really won, Tsubasa.

287
00:17:53,870 --> 00:17:54,790
Yes.

288
00:17:55,260 --> 00:17:57,260
Wakashimazu, we won!

289
00:17:57,260 --> 00:18:01,040
- We won! We won! - Great shot, Tsubasa!

290
00:18:01,130 --> 00:18:03,800
- We advanced to the final! - We did it!

291
00:18:03,880 --> 00:18:05,920
We beat France!

292
00:18:06,010 --> 00:18:08,380
And what a great battle it was.

293
00:18:08,470 --> 00:18:10,590
In this semifinal against France,

294
00:18:10,680 --> 00:18:14,760
the Japan team had to fight with 10 men from the very beginning.

295
00:18:14,850 --> 00:18:17,850
That's why we couldn't see their usual attacking play,

296
00:18:17,930 --> 00:18:20,030
because they focused more on defense.

297
00:18:20,020 --> 00:18:23,440
Japan had to put on a survival game.

298
00:18:23,520 --> 00:18:27,790
And perseverance and a miracle brought them victory!

299
00:18:27,990 --> 00:18:29,740
Yes, we did it!

300
00:18:29,820 --> 00:18:31,660
They advanced to the final!

301
00:18:31,740 --> 00:18:33,910
Just what you'd expect from Tsubasa-senpai.

302
00:18:34,410 --> 00:18:35,550
Tsubasa-kun.

303
00:18:35,550 --> 00:18:37,050
Matsuyama-kun!

304
00:18:37,290 --> 00:18:39,300
Congratulations, Jun!

305
00:18:39,300 --> 00:18:41,180
I drink to all of you!

306
00:18:42,710 --> 00:18:44,590
You were all great, guys!

307
00:18:47,630 --> 00:18:51,940
S-Sorry guys, this is my fault.

308
00:18:52,220 --> 00:18:54,260
It's not your fault.

309
00:18:54,350 --> 00:18:57,640
That's right, Napoleon, it was a great shot.

310
00:18:57,720 --> 00:18:59,810
There was nothing you could do.

311
00:18:59,890 --> 00:19:01,950
Today was his day.

312
00:19:02,520 --> 00:19:03,810
Guys.

313
00:19:06,570 --> 00:19:07,860
Napoleon.

314
00:19:08,900 --> 00:19:12,070
Our football did not end today.

315
00:19:12,530 --> 00:19:14,200
Today, everything begins.

316
00:19:14,870 --> 00:19:17,660
Today, France youth lost.

317
00:19:17,740 --> 00:19:21,370
But this defeat will make us stronger.

318
00:19:21,500 --> 00:19:23,830
French football will become stronger.

319
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:28,630
They will now work harder to beat the golden Japan team.

320
00:19:30,130 --> 00:19:31,090
Misaki.

321
00:19:31,170 --> 00:19:32,100
Pierre.

322
00:19:33,590 --> 00:19:38,720
Our one-on-one duel turned into a team duel, and today we lost.

323
00:19:38,810 --> 00:19:42,110
But our battle has only just begun.

324
00:19:43,730 --> 00:19:44,980
Pierre.

325
00:19:46,230 --> 00:19:51,370
One day I will challenge you again, you'll accept, won't you, Misaki?

326
00:19:51,370 --> 00:19:53,070
Yes, Pierre.

327
00:19:55,570 --> 00:19:58,280
I didn't think Japan would be this strong.

328
00:19:58,370 --> 00:20:00,330
France played very well too.

329
00:20:00,410 --> 00:20:02,290
Both teams fought hard.

330
00:20:02,370 --> 00:20:04,640
Don't let your guard down!

331
00:20:04,920 --> 00:20:06,580
Congratulations, Misaki.

332
00:20:06,790 --> 00:20:11,050
In the final, I will support Japan on your behalf for beating France.

333
00:20:11,550 --> 00:20:17,550
The spectators warmly applaud both teams for their good play.

334
00:20:17,640 --> 00:20:22,400
I can't say it enough, both teams truly put on a magnificent game.

335
00:20:22,600 --> 00:20:23,480
That's right.

336
00:20:23,560 --> 00:20:27,110
To all the people who supported us until the end, even under the rain,

337
00:20:27,190 --> 00:20:28,410
we must say thank you.

338
00:20:28,820 --> 00:20:31,360
Hooray! Hooray!

339
00:20:31,440 --> 00:20:33,670
Oh, they're coming this way.

340
00:20:33,900 --> 00:20:37,420
Thank you for supporting us until the end, friends.

341
00:20:37,660 --> 00:20:38,830
It's nothing.

342
00:20:38,910 --> 00:20:42,700
Good luck in the final, we'll support you.

343
00:20:42,790 --> 00:20:43,930
Thank you.

344
00:20:44,660 --> 00:20:48,680
Schneider, Japan is our opponent in the final.

345
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:49,840
Yes.

346
00:20:49,920 --> 00:20:52,960
But no matter who it is, the result won't change.

347
00:20:54,510 --> 00:20:59,180
We, the Germany youth, will be the winners again.

348
00:21:00,350 --> 00:21:02,520
Roberto, since Japan won,

349
00:21:02,600 --> 00:21:07,100
I will go and make an offer to sign a contract with Tsubasa.

350
00:21:07,440 --> 00:21:11,520
Coach Barbas, who do you think will win the final?

351
00:21:11,650 --> 00:21:14,360
Unfortunately, I think it will be Germany.

352
00:21:14,440 --> 00:21:19,450
Even with Ozora Tsubasa, I doubt Japan can beat Germany.

353
00:21:20,210 --> 00:21:26,210
If Japan wins, won't you talk to Tsubasa?

354
00:21:26,290 --> 00:21:27,220
What?

355
00:21:27,750 --> 00:21:31,920
I want to take him to Brazil first.

356
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:32,980
Roberto!

357
00:21:34,050 --> 00:21:36,590
This is strange, really strange.

358
00:21:36,670 --> 00:21:41,100
The match should have been over long ago, and no one has come yet...

359
00:21:42,810 --> 00:21:43,740
Soda!

360
00:21:44,100 --> 00:21:46,350
We won! We won, Soda!

361
00:21:46,430 --> 00:21:48,140
It went to penalties.

362
00:21:48,230 --> 00:21:51,150
But Wakashimazu saved one and Tsubasa scored, so we won!

363
00:21:51,230 --> 00:21:53,750
Now you'll play in the final!

364
00:21:54,400 --> 00:21:57,780
Guys... I see.

365
00:21:58,820 --> 00:22:00,200
I'm so happy!

366
00:22:00,280 --> 00:22:01,250
Soda.

367
00:22:01,240 --> 00:22:03,330
Idiot, is now the time to cry?

368
00:22:03,410 --> 00:22:06,950
But I've been sitting here alone all this time.

369
00:22:07,040 --> 00:22:08,620
Did you miss us?

370
00:24:46,570 --> 00:24:49,990
NEXT EPISODE: THE LIONS OF THE FINAL!